    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "Conjunctival melanoma",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Sagittal T2-weighted MRI shows a bilobated mass located deep in the right upper eyelid, of intermediate signal intensity on the T1- and T2-weighted images and enhancing. Anteriorly, it invades the orbital septum and almost reaches the orbicularis oculi muscle. Posteriorly, there is orbital invasion, with the tumour invading the levator palpebrae and superior rectus muscles.",
    "source": "Teresa A. Ferreira",
    "copyright": "",
